# LERF-OVS Analysis: THGS vs ReLaGS — Cross-Method Distractor Comparison

> Generated 2026-06-05. Same diagnostic framework applied to both methods on identical LERF-OVS scenes (figurines, ramen, teatime, waldo_kitchen). 67 unique (scene, prompt) pairs, 208 (frame, prompt) rows per method.

---

## 0. Setup

| | THGS | ReLaGS |
|--|--|--|
| Source repo | `/mnt/pilab_nas/projects/THGS` | `/mnt/pilab_nas/projects/ReLaGS` (CVPR 2025, DFKI) |
| Scene model path | `output/lerf/<scene>/` | `output/lerf_hf/scenes/LeRF/<scene>/` (HuggingFace checkpoints) |
| 2DGS iteration | 30000 | 0 (single-pass) |
| Feature aggregation | `if portion < 0.1: continue` skip + L2-norm weighted sum | Multi-view list collect + **outlier-aware aggregation** (cosine sim mean filter, mu - τ·σ) + mean |
| Inference (test) | `test_lerf.py` (canon-contrast topk=3 at level=[2,3]) | Same SemanticNAG class, same inference protocol (we used THGS's renderer for both) |
| Diagnostic CSV | [lerf_ovs_per_prompt.csv](../output/diagnostics/lerf_ovs_per_prompt.csv) | [lerf_ovs_relags.csv](../output/diagnostics/lerf_ovs_relags.csv) |

> **Caveat**: We ran ReLaGS's gaussians through THGS's CUDA rasterizer (different from ReLaGS's `diff-surfel-rasterization-trace-maxcontrib`). Absolute mIoU may not match ReLaGS's reported numbers exactly. However, **per-SP feature analysis (cos_sim, rank, zero-norm)** is rasterizer-independent and fully valid for comparison.

---

## 1. Headline (LangSplat-style aggregation)

| | THGS | ReLaGS | Δ (ReLaGS - THGS) |
|--|--|--|--|
| Oracle mIoU (ceiling) | **0.8072** | **0.8079** | +0.0007 |
| Actual mIoU | **0.5887** | **0.5590** | **-0.0297** |
| Gap (Oracle - Actual) | 0.2185 | **0.2489** | **+0.0304** |

**Observation**: Oracle is nearly identical (both NAGs reach ~0.81 ceiling). **ReLaGS's Actual is 3 points LOWER than THGS** in our protocol, despite their outlier-aware aggregation.

→ The architectural change (outlier filtering) **changes failure distribution but doesn't reduce overall failure rate** in our setup.

### Per-scene breakdown

| Scene | THGS Oracle | THGS Actual | THGS Gap | ReLaGS Oracle | ReLaGS Actual | ReLaGS Gap |
|--|--|--|--|--|--|--|
| figurines | 0.7875 | 0.5493 | 0.2382 | 0.7942 | **0.5641** ↑ | 0.2302 |
| ramen | 0.7784 | 0.4214 | 0.3570 | 0.7857 | **0.3316** ↓ | 0.4541 |
| teatime | 0.9065 | 0.8187 | 0.0878 | 0.9003 | **0.7855** ↓ | 0.1148 |
| waldo_kitchen | 0.7564 | 0.5654 | 0.1909 | 0.7512 | **0.5547** ↓ | 0.1964 |
| **Mean** | 0.8072 | 0.5887 | 0.2185 | 0.8079 | 0.5590 | 0.2489 |

ReLaGS improves on figurines (where THGS had most zero-norm SPs) but degrades on the other 3 scenes.

---

## 2. Zero-norm SP — D1 (Degenerate Distractor) Frequency

ReLaGS's `proj_gaussian_features` uses lower thresholds + zero-fallback, so zero-norm SPs should be reduced.

| Scene | Method | L2 SPs | L2 zero-norm | L2 % | L3 SPs | L3 zero-norm | L3 % |
|--|--|--|--|--|--|--|--|
| figurines | THGS | 546 | **41** | **7.51%** | 199 | **7** | 3.52% |
| figurines | ReLaGS | 463 | **1** ✅ | **0.22%** | 177 | **0** ✅ | 0.00% |
| ramen | THGS | 546 | 3 | 0.55% | 247 | 1 | 0.40% |
| ramen | ReLaGS | 507 | 0 ✅ | 0.00% | 249 | 1 | 0.40% |
| teatime | THGS | 2816 | 32 | 1.14% | 1320 | 15 | 1.14% |
| teatime | ReLaGS | 2630 | 6 ✅ | 0.23% | 1232 | 7 | 0.57% |
| waldo_kitchen | THGS | 1025 | 40 | 3.90% | 424 | 11 | 2.59% |
| waldo_kitchen | ReLaGS | 882 | 3 ✅ | 0.34% | 400 | 3 | 0.75% |

**Total pool-wide zero-norm SP count**:

| Pool (lvl [2,3]) | THGS zero-norm | ReLaGS zero-norm | 감소율 |
|--|--|--|--|
| figurines (745 / 640) | 48 | **1** | **-98%** |
| ramen (793 / 756) | 4 | **1** | -75% |
| teatime (4136 / 3862) | 47 | **13** | -72% |
| waldo_kitchen (1449 / 1282) | 51 | **6** | -88% |
| **Total** | **150** | **21** | **-86%** |

→ ReLaGS의 outlier-aware aggregation은 **D1 (degenerate distractor) 를 86% 감소시킴**. 우리 framework가 정확히 진단한 architectural improvement.

---

## 3. Type A/B/C 분포 — 비교

τ = 0.25 기준:

| | THGS | ReLaGS | Δ |
|--|--|--|--|
| Type C (성공) | 46 (68.7%) | 42 (62.7%) | -4 |
| Type A (CLIP matching 실패) | 20 (29.9%) | **24 (35.8%)** | **+4** |
| Type B (SAM lift 실패) | 1 (1.5%) | 1 (1.5%) | 0 |

**놀라운 발견**: ReLaGS에서 **Type A가 20 → 24로 증가**. 즉 architectural 개선에도 불구하고 **failure prompt 수가 늘었다**.

### Type A IoU 손실 합

| | THGS | ReLaGS | Δ |
|--|--|--|--|
| Type A 손실 합 | 15.48 | **17.14** | **+1.66** |
| Type A 손실 비중 | 85.4% | **87.6%** | +2.2 |

→ ReLaGS는 Type A에 손실이 더 집중되어 있음.

---

## 4. Type A Sub-classification (A1/A2/A3) — 비교

| Sub-type | THGS N | THGS 비중 (of A) | ReLaGS N | ReLaGS 비중 (of A) | Δ |
|--|--|--|--|--|--|
| **A1** (rank ≥ 11) | 12 | 60% | **9** | **37.5%** | -3 (-22.5pp) |
| **A2** (rank 2-10) | 6 | 30% | **12** | **50%** | +6 (+20pp) |
| **A3** (rank = 1) | 2 | 10% | 3 | 12.5% | +1 |

### A1 평균 rank 비교

| | THGS | ReLaGS |
|--|--|--|
| A1 평균 정답 SP rank | **50.3** | **34.3** |
| A2 평균 정답 SP rank | 6.2 | 5.1 |

**해석**:
- ReLaGS는 **A1 (catastrophic ranking failure) 을 12 → 9로 줄임** ✓ (D1 reduction과 일관)
- 그러나 **A2 (moderate ranking failure) 를 6 → 12로 늘림** ✗
- **순효과**: 정답 SP가 더 "가까이" 오긴 함 (A1 ↓, A2 ↑), but topk=3 안에 못 들어오는 prompt는 오히려 늘었음
- ReLaGS의 outlier filter는 **noise뿐만 아니라 일부 정답 신호도 함께 제거**해서 정답 SP rank를 부분적으로 낮춤

